import{_t as e,it as t,n,rt as r}from"./chunks/framework.B5d4da8a.js";var i=JSON.parse(`{"title":"ADR-0120: Paper–Implementation Alignment Plan","description":"","frontmatter":{},"headers":[],"relativePath":"handl/project/adrs/0120-paper-implementation-alignment.md","filePath":"vendored/handl/project/adrs/0120-paper-implementation-alignment.md"}`),a={name:`handl/project/adrs/0120-paper-implementation-alignment.md`};function o(n,i,a,o,s,c){return e(),r(`div`,null,[...i[0]||=[t(`<h1 id="adr-0120-paper–implementation-alignment-plan" tabindex="-1">ADR-0120: Paper–Implementation Alignment Plan <a class="header-anchor" href="#adr-0120-paper–implementation-alignment-plan" aria-label="Permalink to “ADR-0120: Paper–Implementation Alignment Plan”">​</a></h1><h2 id="status" tabindex="-1">Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#status" aria-label="Permalink to “Status”">​</a></h2><p>Accepted — direction decided in review; execution is phased below.</p><p>Refines <a href="./0119-n-dimensional-arrow-calculus.html">ADR-0119 N-Dimensional Arrow Calculus</a> and <code>research/PAPER.md</code>. Supersedes the lambda-flavoured &quot;arrows as closures&quot; proposal considered and rejected in the same review.</p><h2 id="context" tabindex="-1">Context <a class="header-anchor" href="#context" aria-label="Permalink to “Context”">​</a></h2><p><code>research/PAPER.md</code> describes the target architecture: <code>M[n]&lt;A,B&gt;</code> dimension-polymorphic morphisms, laws as higher morphisms, <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[k]</code> axis-parameterized composition, <code>Family</code>/<code>Π</code>/<code>Σ</code>, and effects as higher cells. The <code>Term</code> kernel (<code>plugin-engine/src/term.rs</code>: <code>Arr</code>, <code>Const</code>, <code>Op</code>, <code>Seq</code>, <code>First</code>, <code>Choice</code>, <code>Loop</code>, <code>App</code>, <code>Handle</code>; <code>dim: Box&lt;Term&gt;</code> on <code>Arr</code>/<code>Op</code>) embodies the shape but has gaps that surfaced as concrete failures:</p><ul><li><code>module_returns_closure</code> and the <code>Nat.rec</code> self-application (<code>inner(inner)</code> in <code>desugar.data</code>&#39;s <code>build_recursor</code>) fail because the calculus cannot apply an arrow to an arrow-value.</li><li><code>option_b</code>/<code>path_transport</code> expose hardcoded per-dimension ops (<code>cell_comp_h</code>, <code>cell_comp_v</code>, <code>whisker_*</code>, <code>cell_id</code>, <code>witness</code>, <code>refine</code>) that violate the single-calculus rule.</li><li>The <code>dim</code> field doubles as an effect-grade string for <code>handle</code> routing and a morphism-dimension index — two concepts in one slot.</li></ul><p>Three decisions from the design review drive the plan:</p><ol><li><strong>The language is a pure arrow/combinator calculus.</strong> No lambdas, no closures, no currying. There are no free variables to capture: the lowerer&#39;s <code>env</code> is compile-time substitution into products/projections (<code>id</code>/<code>proj_child</code>), not runtime scope. An &quot;arrow value&quot; is a quoted <code>Term</code> (<code>arr(Term)</code>); application is <code>app</code>; recursion is <code>loop</code>.</li><li><strong>Laws are proof-relevant (&quot;weak&quot;) cells, not erased equalities.</strong><code>α : f ~[2]~&gt; g</code> is a first-class value composable via <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[k]</code> and relatable via <code>~[3]~&gt;</code>. (<code>law_inference</code> normalization remains as the strict fast-path where a canonical form suffices.)</li><li><strong>Cell shape is globular.</strong> <code>M[n]&lt;A,B&gt;</code> with <code>A,B ∈ M[n-1]</code> is already the globular presentation, matches the directed/non-invertible nature of computations and rewrites, and requires no new cell vocabulary. Cubical Kan structure (<code>hcomp</code>, <code>transport</code>, <code>Equiv</code>) is deferred: it is only needed for univalence-style <em>computing</em> equality, which fits an ∞-groupoid fragment better than the general directed calculus.</li></ol><p>A fourth consequence follows from 1–3: <strong>Kan filling is generalized composition.</strong> In a weak globular setting, &quot;every composable pasting diagram has a composite&quot; is the Kan condition — so <code>hcomp</code> is not a new primitive. <code>compose(pasting_diagram)</code> (the n-ary generalization of <code>Seq</code>) covers it:</p><table tabindex="0"><thead><tr><th>Hardcoded op</th><th>Becomes</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><code>cell_comp_h</code> / <code>cell_comp_v</code></td><td><code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[0]</code> / <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[1]</code> — binary <code>compose</code></td></tr><tr><td><code>whisker_left</code> / <code>whisker_right</code></td><td><code>id &gt;&gt;&gt;[k] α</code> — derived, not an op</td></tr><tr><td><code>cell_id</code></td><td><code>id</code> — already primitive</td></tr><tr><td><code>hcomp</code></td><td><code>compose(open_diagram)</code> — general case</td></tr></tbody></table><h2 id="decision" tabindex="-1">Decision <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision”">​</a></h2><p>Execute the alignment in five phases; ordering is load-bearing: <code>1 → 2 → 3 → (4, 5 in parallel)</code>.</p><h3 id="phase-1-—-arrows-as-values" tabindex="-1">Phase 1 — Arrows as values <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-1-—-arrows-as-values" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 1 — Arrows as values”">​</a></h3><ol><li>A <code>function</code> used as a <em>value</em> lowers to <code>Arr { value: &lt;Term&gt; }</code> (quote). No environment is captured — it was already resolved at lower time.</li><li><code>call(f, x)</code> lowers to <code>seq(pair(quote f, x), app)</code> for env-bound <code>f</code>; <code>seq(x, f)</code> remains the encoding of flow <code>x &gt;&gt;&gt; f</code>.</li><li><code>desugar.data</code>&#39;s recursor is re-encoded as <code>loop(step)</code> feedback instead of <code>inner(inner)</code> self-application (the lambda-calculus encoding).</li><li>No currying. Parameters are products; if partial application is ever proven necessary it is expressed as prefix-splice <code>seq(fanout(const a, id), f)</code> — pure products, no closures.</li></ol><h3 id="phase-2-—-composition-axes" tabindex="-1">Phase 2 — Composition axes <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-2-—-composition-axes" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 2 — Composition axes”">​</a></h3><ol start="5"><li><code>Term::Seq</code> gains an <code>axis</code> slot (default <code>0</code>); <code>f &gt;&gt;&gt; g</code> is <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[0]</code>.</li><li><code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[k]</code> surface syntax is a YAML/grammar change only.</li><li>Types track globular source/target at every level <code>≤ n</code>; the typing rule for <code>a &gt;&gt;&gt;[k] b</code> is <code>tgt_k(a) = src_k(b)</code>.</li></ol><h3 id="phase-3-—-dim-unification" tabindex="-1">Phase 3 — <code>dim</code> unification <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-3-—-dim-unification" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 3 — dim unification”">​</a></h3><ol start="8"><li>Merge <code>ArrSource::Foreign(grade)</code> into morphism dimension; the <code>~[n]~&gt;</code> bracket means dimension. Open sub-question: grades are names and dims are numbers, so handler lookup becomes dimension-typed.</li><li>Effects are re-read as cells: <code>op</code> is a cell, <code>handle</code> a cell interpreter (<code>(N+1)</code>-cell mapping an effectful <code>N</code>-cell to a pure one, per ADR-0119 §6).</li></ol><h3 id="phase-4-—-dependent-structure" tabindex="-1">Phase 4 — Dependent structure <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-4-—-dependent-structure" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 4 — Dependent structure”">​</a></h3><ol start="10"><li><code>Family&lt;A&gt;</code>, <code>Π</code>, <code>Σ</code> enter via <code>types.yaml</code> + <code>desugar</code> — extending the existing <code>data</code>/indexed-family/recursor machinery.</li><li>Reindexing <code>f*</code> is composition (<code>· &gt;&gt;&gt; f</code>); <code>Σ_f ⊣ f* ⊣ Π_f</code> is expressed as laws (<code>~[2]~&gt;</code> cells), not engine primitives.</li></ol><h3 id="phase-5-—-laws-as-m-2-terms" tabindex="-1">Phase 5 — Laws as <code>M[2]</code> terms <a class="header-anchor" href="#phase-5-—-laws-as-m-2-terms" aria-label="Permalink to “Phase 5 — Laws as M[2] terms”">​</a></h3><ol start="12"><li><code>f ~[2]~&gt; g</code> parses to a <code>Term</code> and feeds <code>law_inference</code> — no separate laws fragment.</li><li><code>Path</code>/<code>Equiv</code>/<code>Refine</code>/<code>witness</code>/<code>cell_*</code>/<code>whisker_*</code> are <strong>derived arrows</strong> (interchange + <code>compose</code>), not engine primitives; the <code>option_b</code> op surface collapses into the generic combinators.</li></ol><h3 id="decision-gates" tabindex="-1">Decision gates <a class="header-anchor" href="#decision-gates" aria-label="Permalink to “Decision gates”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Strict vs weak:</strong> resolved — weak (proof-relevant). <code>law_inference</code> stays as the strict fast-path.</li><li><strong>Globular vs cubical:</strong> resolved — globular. Reopen only if univalence- computing equality becomes a requirement; then as a cube-diagram fragment, not a rewrite.</li></ul><h2 id="consequences" tabindex="-1">Consequences <a class="header-anchor" href="#consequences" aria-label="Permalink to “Consequences”">​</a></h2><ul><li><strong>Fixes unblocked by Phase 1:</strong> <code>module_returns_closure</code>, <code>data_recursor_step_case_one</code>, <code>data_recursor_recurse_depth_two</code>, and the <code>indexed_family_*</code> recursor paths — all currently blocked on arrow-application-of-arrows.</li><li><strong>Ops removed, not added:</strong> <code>cell_comp_*</code>, <code>whisker_*</code>, <code>cell_id</code>, <code>hcomp</code>-style ops fold into <code>compose</code>/<code>&gt;&gt;&gt;</code>/<code>id</code> — one generic combinator replaces ~5 hardcoded ones, per the single-calculus rule.</li><li><strong><code>eval_rec</code>/<code>rec</code> region:</strong> superseded by <code>loop</code>-encoded recursion where the fixpoint is structural; the region form may remain for general fixpoint blocks.</li><li><strong>Deferred:</strong> cubical Kan (<code>transport</code>/<code>Equiv</code> computing), strictness metatheory, per-axis coherence proofs.</li><li><strong>Known debt:</strong> <code>lower_ast</code>&#39;s <code>match node.kind</code> table (ADR-0105) remains hardcoded pending a <code>lower</code> scheme fragment per <code>AstShapeDef</code>; the typecheck model&#39;s fuel circuit breaker is tactical, not a fix.</li></ul><h2 id="implementation-status" tabindex="-1">Implementation Status <a class="header-anchor" href="#implementation-status" aria-label="Permalink to “Implementation Status”">​</a></h2><p>All five phases have landed on <code>main</code>. The residual items below are documented approximations and deferrals, not phase regressions.</p><ul><li><strong>Phase 1 — arrows as values: done</strong> (<code>2751b84e</code>). <code>function</code>-as-value lowers to a quoted <code>Arr{value: Term}</code>; <code>call(f, x)</code> lowers to <code>pair(quote f, x) &gt;&gt;&gt; app</code>; capturing nested functions lower to bound-arrow records <code>{__term__, __bound__}</code> — products, no closures. <code>desugar.data</code> recursors are <code>loop</code> fold machines over defunctionalized work stacks (<code>ast.loop</code>/<code>eval.loop</code> shapes); the lambda-style <code>inner(inner)</code> self-application is gone.</li><li><strong>Phase 2 — composition axes: done</strong> (<code>907fee4f</code>, <code>9aa7d2c7</code>, <code>95ffaa7b</code>). <code>Term::Seq{axis, fst, snd}</code> (serde-defaulted axis); <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[k]</code> is pure YAML (<code>ast.axis_flow</code> <code>left</code>/<code>axis</code>/<code>right</code> roles, <code>eval.axis_flow</code>, <code>type.axis_flow</code>); <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;</code> is <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[0]</code>. For <code>k &gt; 0</code> the term executes as globular paste <code>∘ₖ</code> via <code>cell2_comp_axis</code> with <code>tgt_k = src_k</code> enforcement; <code>Term::globular_dim</code> gates <code>k &lt; dim</code>; all compile backends are dimension-aware. At the type level <code>A ~[N]~&gt; B</code> synthesizes <code>Arrow{inputs, grade, output, dim}</code> and <code>synth_axis_flow</code>/<code>synth_dim_arrow</code> implement the boundary law via <code>cell_boundary_</code>/<code>cell_paste_</code>/<code>axis_flow_compose_</code>.</li><li><strong>Phase 3 — <code>dim</code> unification: done</strong> (<code>f6927434</code>). A grade is a named dimension (<code>Const &quot;S&quot;</code>) in the shared <code>dim</code> slot; <code>ArrSource::Foreign</code> is the host-function boundary only; handler routing is dimension-typed (<code>substitute_capability</code> matches dims).</li><li><strong>Phase 4 — dependent structure: done</strong> (<code>f9f6da22</code>, <code>f7761384</code>). <code>handl-packages/type/dependent.hnl</code>: <code>reindex := (f, P) ~&gt; f &gt;&gt;&gt; P</code>; the <code>Σ_f ⊣ f* ⊣ Π_f</code> unit/counit laws are <code>~[2]~&gt;</code> terms. The model recognizes <code>Family</code>/<code>Pi</code>/<code>Sigma</code>/<code>Forall</code>; <code>data</code> binds <code>type.family</code>/ <code>type.family_app</code>; <code>type.ctor_sig</code> instantiates per use (<code>Succ(3)</code> rejects); index terms normalize computationally (<code>1+1</code>≡<code>2</code>, commutative canonicalization, ring identities, linear <code>Bin</code>-solving); <code>match</code> patterns bind constructor fields.</li><li><strong>Phase 5 — laws as <code>M[2]</code> terms: done</strong> (<code>f4016e65</code>). <code>~[2]~&gt;</code> mints a genuine dimension-2 <code>Op</code> feeding <code>law_inference</code>/<code>quantified_laws</code> directly — no separate laws fragment. <code>cell_comp_h</code>/<code>cell_comp_v</code> are <code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[0]</code>/<code>&gt;&gt;&gt;[1]</code> at dim 2, <code>whisker_*</code> is <code>id₂ ∘₀ α</code>, <code>cell_id</code> is <code>id</code> — all derived schemes in <code>eval.yaml</code>; <code>Term::Opaque</code> folds unrecognized derived operators to tagged records. <code>option_b</code>, <code>path_transport</code>, and <code>model_infrastructure</code> are green.</li></ul><p>Supporting work on the same arc: <code>bad3d1c4</code> (typecheck model <code>RecordProj</code> resolution; graduated predicate guarantees — Proven / Blocked→ <code>runtime_assert</code> / Refuted), <code>167a18ab</code> (scheme-driven lowering — <code>lower_via_scheme</code>/<code>instantiate_scheme</code>; YAML-declared constructs lower with zero Rust arms; <code>input_faithful</code> tracking, <code>seq_pastes</code> globular pasting), <code>6913ef61</code> (<code>pattern_role</code>/<code>pattern_role_is</code> accessors; kind dispatch in pattern-match/tree-walk/bytecode/cranelift migrated to <code>AstShapeDef</code> roles).</p><h3 id="deferred-residual" tabindex="-1">Deferred / residual <a class="header-anchor" href="#deferred-residual" aria-label="Permalink to “Deferred / residual”">​</a></h3><ul><li><strong>Dependent elimination / index refinement</strong> — <code>match</code> binds fields but does not refine the scrutinee&#39;s family index per arm; true dependent elimination needs an equality type/proof term (<code>v ≡ Ctor …</code>).</li><li><strong><code>unify</code> shallow for <code>type.function</code></strong> — dependent-aware unification lives in <code>unify_dependent_</code>; a composite <code>f &gt;&gt;&gt; P</code> of dependent operands flattens to <code>type.function</code> (no AST body to carry a <code>body_closure</code> across composition).</li><li><strong><code>cell_boundary_</code> assumes globularity</strong> — the globe condition <code>src_j(inputs) = src_j(output)</code> is assumed, not verified.</li><li><s><strong>Optional-role support in <code>AstShapeDef</code></strong></s> — landed: <code>ChildRoleSpec</code> gains <code>optional: true</code>, <code>AstShapeDef::role_index_at</code> / <code>Language::child_role_index_for</code> resolve arity-aware, and <code>match</code> (<code>motive</code>) / <code>assign</code> (<code>body</code>) declare optional roles in <code>ast.yaml</code>. The tree-walk/bytecode/cranelift <code>match</code> arms, tree-walk <code>assign</code> body, arrow-lower let-form, and <code>desugar.match_recursor</code> all consume the roles.</li><li><strong><code>k ≥ 2</code> rejected</strong> — <code>Cell2</code> is the only cell shape the value model carries; axes beyond 1 fail <code>k &lt; dim</code> and the typechecker diagnoses them unconditionally.</li><li><strong>Cubical Kan</strong> (<code>transport</code>/<code>Equiv</code> computing) — deferred per the decision above; reopen only for univalence-computing equality, as a cube-diagram fragment.</li><li><strong>Lowerer <code>match node.kind</code> table</strong> — reduced, not eliminated: the env/substitution constructs (<code>function</code>, <code>call</code>, <code>assign</code>, <code>flow</code>, …) keep Rust arms; YAML-declared schemes lower generically via <code>lower_via_scheme</code>.</li><li><strong><code>desugar.data</code>/<code>desugar.match_recursor</code></strong> — remain semantic natives (constructor iteration, strict positivity, arena search); the <code>rec</code> region form is retained for self-referential fixpoints.</li></ul>`,33)]])}var s=n(a,[[`render`,o]]);export{i as __pageData,s as default};